#AUTO 16
#NEEDED 0
# CPU core recon (issue 110n / phase-2 prep) — gather once, then de-select.
#
# Reads the boot core's fixed identity and current execution state via the
# system registers: MIDR (core type/revision), MPIDR (which physical core we
# booted on), CurrentEL (which exception level), and SCTLR (whether the MMU
# and data cache are on — expected OFF in phase 1). The identity is fixed
# silicon: gather it once, record it in the hardware docs, then set #NEEDED 0.
#
# The other three cores' STATE (parked where?) cannot be read from here
# without waking them — that belongs to phase-2 multi-core bring-up, where a
# fresh probe confirms the wake landed. System registers -> MRS, done in C.

CALL cpu_recon
